---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, legalEntity } from '~/lib/site';
const updated = '2026-05-05';
const entity = legalEntity;
---

<Base
  title="Cancellation & Refund Policy"
  description={`Cancellation and refund policy for ${entity.name} digital product purchases on ${site.domain}.`}
  pageType="WebPage"
  noindex={false}
>
  <section class="container-app py-20 max-w-prose-tight">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal · Global</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4">Cancellation &amp; Refund Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-subtle text-fluid-sm">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-subtle text-fluid-sm">
      Applicable to purchases made on the global variant of {site.domain} (USD pricing, Stripe checkout). For purchases on the India variant, see the <a href="/in/legal/refund" class="text-brand">India refund policy</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="prose mt-10 text-muted [&_h2]:text-fg [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_h2]:text-fluid-xl [&_p]:my-3 [&_strong]:text-fg [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6 [&_li]:my-1.5 [&_a]:text-brand">

      <h2>1. Nature of the products</h2>
      <p>
        All products sold by <strong>{entity.name}</strong> through
        <code>{site.domain}</code> are <strong>digital products</strong>
        — source-code repositories, configuration packages, and access
        to a private community channel — delivered electronically
        immediately on payment confirmation. They are not physical
        goods (see our separate
        <a href="/legal/shipping">Shipping &amp; Exchange Policy</a>).
      </p>

      <h2>2. Cancellation</h2>
      <p>
        Because delivery is automatic and immediate, an order
        <strong>cannot be cancelled</strong> after the Stripe payment
        is captured and the buyer has been granted access to the
        purchased repository or community channel. If You initiated a
        payment but it has not yet been captured, no further action is
        needed — the authorisation will expire and no funds will be
        debited.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Refund — free Vibe Coder Kit</h2>
      <p>
        The free Vibe Coder Kit involves no payment and therefore
        carries no refund. You may unsubscribe from associated
        communications at any time using the unsubscribe link in any
        marketing email or by writing to
        <a href={`mailto:${entity.email}`}> {entity.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Refund — individual paid agents (BSK-001 to BSK-006)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Eligible for a <strong>full refund within 14 days</strong> of purchase.</li>
        <li>Reason is not required, though a one-line explanation helps us improve.</li>
        <li>Request the refund by replying to Your Stripe receipt or by emailing <a href={`mailto:${entity.email}`}>{entity.email}</a> from the email address used at checkout.</li>
        <li>After 14 days, no refunds are issued, in line with the digital-goods nature of the Service.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Refund — AI Digital Marketing Stack bundle (BSK-ALL)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Eligible for a <strong>full refund within 7 days</strong> of purchase. The shorter window reflects the substantially higher value at risk on bundle purchases where the entire six-agent source delivery is granted immediately.</li>
        <li>Same request channel as individual agents (reply to Stripe receipt or email <a href={`mailto:${entity.email}`}>{entity.email}</a>).</li>
        <li>After 7 days, the bundle is non-refundable.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. How refunds are processed</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Approved refunds are issued via Stripe back to <strong>the original payment instrument</strong> only — the credit or debit card used at checkout. We cannot redirect a refund to a different instrument.</li>
        <li>Refund initiation typically takes <strong>1 business day</strong> from approval; settlement to Your card statement typically takes a further <strong>5 to 10 business days</strong> depending on the issuing bank's cycle.</li>
        <li>You will receive a Stripe refund-confirmation email containing the refund reference. If the funds do not appear within 14 business days of that email, contact <a href={`mailto:${entity.email}`}>{entity.email}</a> and we will follow up with Stripe.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>7. Effect of refund</h2>
      <p>
        On any refund being approved and initiated, the following
        consequences take effect immediately:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your access to the private GitHub repository for the refunded SKU is revoked.</li>
        <li>Your role in the Glitch Grow Discord server (<code>@Agent Buyer</code> or <code>@AI Digital Marketing Stack Buyer</code>) is removed and access to the corresponding paid channels is closed.</li>
        <li>Your entitlement to lifetime updates for the refunded SKU is terminated.</li>
        <li>The Business Source License 1.1 ("BSL") under which the agent was delivered <strong>terminates</strong> with effect from the refund date. Any continued use, deployment, or onward delivery of the previously-licensed source after that date constitutes infringement.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Disputes &amp; chargebacks</h2>
      <p>
        Before initiating a card chargeback, please contact us at
        <a href={`mailto:${entity.email}`}> {entity.email}</a> — we
        will issue a refund directly per Sections 4 and 5 above
        wherever Your request falls within the eligibility window.
        If a chargeback is filed against an ineligible transaction,
        we will contest it with Stripe using the records of access
        delivery (repository invitation, Discord role assignment, IP
        and timestamp logs).
      </p>

      <h2>9. Statutory rights</h2>
      <p>
        Where mandatory consumer-protection statute in Your
        jurisdiction (for example, Ontario's Consumer Protection Act,
        2002, the EU Consumer Rights Directive 2011/83/EU, or the UK
        Consumer Rights Act 2015) grants You broader cancellation
        rights than this Policy, those statutory rights are not
        diminished by anything in this document. Where the digital
        goods exception applies (e.g. EU CRD Art. 16(m) — supply of
        digital content not on a tangible medium where performance
        has begun with consent), the Policy windows above govern
        instead.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact &amp; escalation</h2>
      <p>
        For any question regarding cancellation or refund:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email</strong>: <a href={`mailto:${entity.email}`}>{entity.email}</a></li>
        <li><strong>Postal address</strong>: {entity.name}, attention {entity.owner}, {entity.address}</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>11. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        This Policy is governed by the laws of {entity.jurisdiction}
        and the federal laws of Canada applicable therein. Disputes
        are subject to the dispute-resolution mechanism in our
        <a href="/legal/terms"> Terms of Service</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
